course: dictionary
lesson: 10045
title: One word, more than one meaning
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning. «Terrier» can be a kind of dog, or it can describe a person. To find the right meaning, look at the words around it, which is the context.
explain: Read this sentence: «That is how we got sheepdogs that herd, terriers that dig after rats, retrievers that bring back birds from water, hounds that follow a scent and greyhounds built to sprint.» Sheepdogs, retrievers, hounds and greyhounds are all dog types, so terriers must be a dog type too.
explain: Now read about sport: a player who chases every ball is «a real terrier». Nobody means a dog here. Try the dog meaning in the sentence and it does not fit, but the meaning "a person who is very determined and does not give up" fits perfectly.
fact: A terrier is a small or medium-sized, lively dog first bred to hunt and dig out small animals such as rats, rabbits and foxes.
fact: Terriers are energetic, brave and love to dig.
fact: Famous terrier breeds include the Jack Russell, the Scottie (Scottish terrier), the Westie, the Yorkshire terrier and the Irish terrier.
fact: A person can be called a terrier, meaning very determined and never giving up.
exercise: «Kieran's nan's terrier Mitzi has bitten two people, so she wears a muzzle when visitors come.» What kind of thing is a terrier here? | A kind of food | A cup of tea | *A dog | A house
exercise: Sport talk: a player who chases every ball is «a real terrier». What does terrier mean here? | A ball that bounces high | A small, lively dog that digs | *A person who is very determined and never gives up | A player who is slow and lazy
exercise: «Sheepdogs herd, terriers dig after rats, retrievers carry back shot birds gently in soft mouths.» What is the terrier's job? | To follow a scent | To herd sheep | To carry birds from the water | *To dig after rats
test: Which of these is a terrier breed? | Greyhound | Labrador | Poodle | *Westie
test: «Alice then praises a farmer's terrier that "kills all the rats".» What is the terrier doing in this story? | Herding cows | *Killing rats | Swimming in the river | Fetching newspapers
exam: A coach shouts, «Be a terrier out there!» What does he want the team to do? | Sleep more before the match | Chase only the big balls | Give up quickly when it gets hard | *Keep going and never give up
